  @('Reality Glitch: The Fractured Eye','Two panels side by side on one image, divided down the middle. LEFT PANEL: the tattoo design alone on a plain white background, shown flat exactly as described, no body, drawn large so it fills most of the panel. RIGHT PANEL: Studio photograph of a real person''s body showing the same exact tattoo where described, healed tattoo on real skin in soft even light, the rest of the body modestly covered by simple plain clothing, only the tattooed area bare, plain seamless light grey studio backdrop - no room, no furniture, no scenery. The tattoo in both panels is identical. The tattoo: The Fractured Eye - a realistic eye containing several incompatible realities. Each section of the iris reveals a different world, with architecture, landscapes, and celestial structures arranged around the pupil. A Reality Glitch tattoo in surreal colour realism. No text, labels, logos or watermarks in the tattoo. In the right panel it is on a man, outer forearm, a medium tattoo about the size of his hand, with plenty of bare skin around it.'),
  @('Elemental Fusion: The Dual Wolf','Two panels side by side on one image, divided down the middle. LEFT PANEL: the tattoo design alone on a plain white background, shown flat exactly as described, no body, drawn large so it fills most of the panel. RIGHT PANEL: Studio photograph of a real person''s body showing the same exact tattoo where described, healed tattoo on real skin in soft even light, the rest of the body modestly covered by simple plain clothing, only the tattooed area bare, plain seamless light grey studio backdrop - no room, no furniture, no scenery. The tattoo in both panels is identical. The tattoo: The Dual Wolf - a powerful wolf whose anatomy transitions between fire and ice. One side has flowing ember-like fur, glowing cracks, and smoky tendrils. The other side has crystalline fur, frost-covered whiskers, and translucent ice structures. The transition must follow the wolf''s actual anatomy rather than creating an arbitrary split down the middle. The eyes should feel like two expressions of the same intelligent creature. An Elemental Fusion tattoo in colour realism. No text, labels, logos or watermarks in the tattoo. In the right panel it is on a man, outer upper arm, a medium-to-large tattoo that still sits well inside that area, not a full sleeve.'),
  @('Elemental Fusion: The Rain Bear','Two panels side by side on one image, divided down the middle. LEFT PANEL: the tattoo design alone on a plain white background, shown flat exactly as described, no body, drawn large so it fills most of the panel. RIGHT PANEL: Studio photograph of a real person''s body showing the same exact tattoo where described, healed tattoo on real skin in soft even light, the rest of the body modestly covered by simple plain clothing, only the tattooed area bare, plain seamless light grey studio backdrop - no room, no furniture, no scenery. The tattoo in both panels is identical. The tattoo: The Rain Bear - a massive bear whose fur transitions into cascading rain. Its shoulders contain dark storm clouds, while individual droplets form the outline of its limbs. Use a strong silhouette and restrained detail. An Elemental Fusion tattoo in black-and-grey realism. No text, labels, logos or watermarks in the tattoo. In the right panel it is on a man, outer forearm, a medium tattoo about the size of his hand, with plenty of bare skin around it.')
